.TH std::unstoppable_token 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::unstoppable_token \- std::unstoppable_token

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <stop_token>
template< class Token >

concept unstoppable_token =
std::stoppable_token<Token> &&                               (since C++26)
requires (const Token tok) {
requires std::bool_constant<(!tok.stop_possible())>::value;

};

The concept unstoppable_token<Token> specifies an additional requirement for a
stoppable_token where the type does not allow stopping. That is, the expression
tok.stop_possible() must be usable in constant expression and returns false.
